{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019s9SXEjtpBTW2qTvwY6mpJ","type":"tool_result","content":"{\r\n  \"id\": \"US-178\",\r\n  \"title\": \"Add CSS print stylesheet for booking confirmation and receipt pages\",\r\n  \"priority\": \"low\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Add @media print CSS rules to the booking confirmation and /book pages so guests can print or save-as-PDF a clean, readable booking record. Without print styles, navigation, cookie banners, chat widgets, and booking CTAs clutter the printed output, making the page unusable as a physical or PDF booking reference that guests may need for customs, visa applications, or accommodation proof.\",\r\n  \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\r\n    \"@media print CSS hides navigation, footer, cookie banner, chat widget, sticky booking bar, and all CTAs\",\r\n    \"Booking reference number, dates, room type, price, and hostel full address/contact details are clearly visible when printed\",\r\n    \"All text renders in black (#000) on white (#fff) in print mode \\u2014 no coloured backgrounds consume ink\",\r\n    \"Body font size is at least 12pt for readability on A4 paper\",\r\n    \"Page breaks are avoided within booking summary blocks using page-break-inside: avoid\",\r\n    \"Print preview in Chrome shows a clean, professional 1-page booking confirmation\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"technicalNotes\": [\r\n    \"Add @media print rules to a global CSS file or a dedicated print.css imported in layout.tsx\",\r\n    \"Hide elements: @media print { nav, footer, .cookie-banner, .chat-widget { display: none !important; } }\",\r\n    \"Force monochrome: @media print { * { color: #000 !important; background: transparent !important; } }\",\r\n    \"Tailwind print: variant \\u2014 className='print:hidden' for elements to hide, className='print:block' for print-only elements\",\r\n    \"Reference: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/@media/print\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"dependencies\": [],\r\n  \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\r\n  \"passes\": false,\r\n  \"model\": \"haiku\",\r\n  \"_failureReason\": \"oversized_diff: produced 17126 lines but limit is 500. Keep total insertions+deletions under 500 lines.\",\r\n  \"_antiPatterns\": [\r\n    \"oversized_diff: produced 17126 lines but limit is 500. Keep total insertions+deletions under 500 lines.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"last_attempted\": \"2026-04-14T04:46:06Z\"\r\n}\n[rerun: b1]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ebb097a-576d-4b77-a7a3-7eb4b36c845f","uuid":"f4e8e660-f236-4e67-8e0a-aa948b3e274a","timestamp":"2026-04-14T04:47:20.945Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\r\n  \"id\": \"US-178\",\r\n  \"title\": \"Add CSS print stylesheet for booking confirmation and receipt pages\",\r\n  \"priority\": \"low\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Add @media print CSS rules to the booking confirmation and /book pages so guests can print or save-as-PDF a clean, readable booking record. Without print styles, navigation, cookie banners, chat widgets, and booking CTAs clutter the printed output, making the page unusable as a physical or PDF booking reference that guests may need for customs, visa applications, or accommodation proof.\",\r\n  \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\r\n    \"@media print CSS hides navigation, footer, cookie banner, chat widget, sticky booking bar, and all CTAs\",\r\n    \"Booking reference number, dates, room type, price, and hostel full address/contact details are clearly visible when printed\",\r\n    \"All text renders in black (#000) on white (#fff) in print mode \\u2014 no coloured backgrounds consume ink\",\r\n    \"Body font size is at least 12pt for readability on A4 paper\",\r\n    \"Page breaks are avoided within booking summary blocks using page-break-inside: avoid\",\r\n    \"Print preview in Chrome shows a clean, professional 1-page booking confirmation\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"technicalNotes\": [\r\n    \"Add @media print rules to a global CSS file or a dedicated print.css imported in layout.tsx\",\r\n    \"Hide elements: @media print { nav, footer, .cookie-banner, .chat-widget { display: none !important; } }\",\r\n    \"Force monochrome: @media print { * { color: #000 !important; background: transparent !important; } }\",\r\n    \"Tailwind print: variant \\u2014 className='print:hidden' for elements to hide, className='print:block' for print-only elements\",\r\n    \"Reference: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/@media/print\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"dependencies\": [],\r\n  \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\r\n  \"passes\": false,\r\n  \"model\": \"haiku\",\r\n  \"_failureReason\": \"oversized_diff: produced 17126 lines but limit is 500. Keep total insertions+deletions under 500 lines.\",\r\n  \"_antiPatterns\": [\r\n    \"oversized_diff: produced 17126 lines but limit is 500. Keep total insertions+deletions under 500 lines.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"last_attempted\": \"2026-04-14T04:46:06Z\"\r\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D5d3Any6cBv6QhdMHu9hSX","type":"tool_result","content":"2.  **Convert to Popover API:**\r\n    *   Add the `popover` attribute to the tooltip container element (e.g., `<div popover=\"auto\">...</div>`).\r\n    *   Change the trigger element (the button or element that shows the tooltip) to use the `popovertarget` attribute, pointing to the ID of the popover container.\r\n    *   Remove the existing JavaScript logic that manually shows/hides the tooltip.\r\n3.  **Implement CSS Anchor Positioning:**\r\n    *   On the trigger element, assign a unique `anchor-name` via CSS (e.g., `anchor-name: --my-tooltip-trigger;`).\r\n    *   On the popover element, use `position-anchor: --my-tooltip-trigger;` to link it to the trigger.\r\n    *   Use `inset-area` or fallback positioning (`top`, `left`) to position the popover relative to the anchor.\r\n4.  **Fallback for Older Browsers:** Wrap the anchor positioning CSS in an `@supports (position-anchor: --anchor-name)` block. Provide a basic `position: absolute;` fallback for browsers that don't support it.\r\n5.  **Clean Up:** Remove the Popper.js or equivalent dependency from `package.json` and run `npm install` to reduce the bundle size.\r\n\r\n**Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\r\n\r\n*   **Browser Support:** The Popover API is widely supported, but CSS Anchor Positioning is very new (Chrome 125+). The fallback CSS is critical for Firefox, Safari, and older Chrome versions.\r\n*   **Complex Positioning:** For tooltips that need to flip their position based on viewport collision, the new APIs do not yet have a built-in \"auto\" placement like Popper.js. The implementation might need to handle a few common positions manually (e.g., top, bottom).\r\n*   **Styling Conflicts:** The popover element is promoted to the top layer, which can affect existing `z-index` and positioning styles. Test thoroughly to ensure it doesn't appear underneath other elements.\r\n\r\n## Iteration 1 - Tue, Apr 14, 2026  8:55:18 AM\r\nFAILED diff-guard: Add Pinterest Rich Pins metadata for room and blog pages (ID: US-159) — 14223 lines > 500 limit — attempt 1/3\r\n\r\n\r\n## Iteration US-159 - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\r\n\r\nCompleted: Add Pinterest Rich Pins metadata for room and blog pages (ID: US-159)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- `site/src/app/layout.tsx`: Added Pinterest domain verification meta tag (`p:domain_verify`) using `NEXT_PUBLIC_PINTEREST_VERIFICATION_TOKEN` env var\r\n- `site/src/app/rooms/page.tsx`: Added `other` metadata block with `og:price:amount`, `og:price:currency`, `product:price:amount`, `product:price:currency` for Pinterest Product Rich Pin\r\n- `site/src/app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx`: Fixed `publishedTime` to use `new Date(post.date).toISOString()` ensuring ISO 8601 format\r\n- `site/src/app/guide/page.tsx`: Changed `type` from \"website\" to \"article\" and added `publishedTime` in ISO 8601 format\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- Most of the acceptance criteria were already satisfied from prior work; the key missing piece was Pinterest domain verification in the root layout\r\n- Previous attempt (14223 lines) catastrophically exceeded the diff limit — solution was to recognize what's already done and make only the minimal missing change\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- First attempt failed with 14,223 lines > 500 limit. Only 35 lines of actual changes needed.\r\n- Pinterest domain verification token is injected via `NEXT_PUBLIC_PINTEREST_VERIFICATION_TOKEN` env var (set in Vercel dashboard)\r\n## Iteration 2 - Tue, Apr 14, 2026  9:01:31 AM\r\nFAILED diagnosis-block gate: Add Pinterest Rich Pins metadata for room and blog pages (ID: US-159) — no diagnosis block found — attempt 2/3\r\n\r\n\r\n## Iteration US-160 - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\r\n\r\nCompleted: Enable Turbopack file system caching for faster development cold starts (ID: US-160)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- Added `turbopackFileSystemCacheForDev: true` to the `experimental` config object in `site/next.config.ts`\r\n- Added explanatory comment documenting the feature (Turbopack file system caching for faster development cold starts)\r\n- Configuration is on lines 44-46 in next.config.ts\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- Turbopack file system caching is a simple one-line config change in Next.js 16\r\n- The `.next/` directory (including `.next/cache/`) is already excluded from git via root `.gitignore`\r\n- No additional code changes required beyond the config change\r\n\r\n### Test results\r\n- TypeScript compilation: ✓ passes (npx tsc --noEmit)\r\n- Git commit: ✓ successful (d436793)\r\n- Acceptance criteria met:\r\n  - ✓ turbopackFileSystemCacheForDev: true added to experimental config\r\n  - ✓ .next/cache directory already excluded from git\r\n  - ✓ TypeScript compiles without errors\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- None observed; straightforward configuration change\r\n## Iteration 2 - Tue, Apr 14, 2026  9:22:17 AM\r\nFAILED diff-guard: Implement React 19.2 useEffectEvent for stable analytics event handlers (ID: US-161) — 540 lines > 500 limit — attempt 1/3\r\n\r\n## Iteration 1 - Tue, Apr 14, 2026  9:22:20 AM\r\nCompleted: Enable Turbopack file system caching for faster development cold starts (ID: US-160) in 12m\r\n\r\n## Iteration 1 - Tue, Apr 14, 2026  9:37:20 AM\r\nFAILED diff-guard: Implement React 19.2 useEffectEvent for stable analytics event handlers (ID: US-161) — 23068 lines > 500 limit — attempt 2/3\r\n\r\n\r\n## Iteration US-161 - Tue, Apr 14, 2026\r\n\r\nCompleted: Implement React 19.2 useEffectEvent for stable analytics event handlers (ID: US-161)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- `site/src/components/RoomsEcommerceTracker.tsx`: Replaced `useCallback` with `useEffectEvent` for the analytics click handler\r\n  - Changed import: `useCallback` → `useEffectEvent`\r\n  - Changed `useCallback((e) => {...}, [])` → `useEffectEvent((e) => {...})`\r\n  - Changed deps from `[handleClick]` → `[]` with comment \"handleClick is an Effect Event — not a dependency\"\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- `RoomsEcommerceTracker.tsx` was the right target: it had `useCallback` for an analytics-only function in `useEffect` deps\r\n- `BookEcommerceTracker.tsx` already used `useEffectEvent` (from US-163/US-169), so it was already done\r\n- Write via Bash heredoc required — Edit tool changes didn't persist to disk (Windows path encoding issue between tool and filesystem)\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- Previous attempt (540 lines) likely created a new file or made sweeping changes — minimal approach (one file, ~12 line diff) is the right strategy\r\n- Edit tool applied changes to in-memory Read cache but NOT to disk — must verify with `cat` and use Bash heredoc to write if needed\r\n## Iteration 1 - Tue, Apr 14, 2026  9:42:43 AM\r\nFAILED diagnosis-block gate: Implement React 19.2 useEffectEvent for stable analytics event handlers (ID: US-161) — no diagnosis block found — attempt 3/3\r\n\r\n## Iteration 1 - Tue, Apr 14, 2026 12:46:02 PM\nFAILED diff-guard: Add CSS print stylesheet for booking confirmation and receipt pages (ID: US-178) — 17126 lines > 500 limit — attempt 1/3\n[rerun: b2]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ebb097a-576d-4b77-a7a3-7eb4b36c845f","uuid":"bc0e18f0-9b85-4469-a3c2-ad6d887bc6da","timestamp":"2026-04-14T04:47:41.247Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"2.  **Convert to Popover API:**\r\n    *   Add the `popover` attribute to the tooltip container element (e.g., `<div popover=\"auto\">...</div>`).\r\n    *   Change the trigger element (the button or element that shows the tooltip) to use the `popovertarget` attribute, pointing to the ID of the popover container.\r\n    *   Remove the existing JavaScript logic that manually shows/hides the tooltip.\r\n3.  **Implement CSS Anchor Positioning:**\r\n    *   On the trigger element, assign a unique `anchor-name` via CSS (e.g., `anchor-name: --my-tooltip-trigger;`).\r\n    *   On the popover element, use `position-anchor: --my-tooltip-trigger;` to link it to the trigger.\r\n    *   Use `inset-area` or fallback positioning (`top`, `left`) to position the popover relative to the anchor.\r\n4.  **Fallback for Older Browsers:** Wrap the anchor positioning CSS in an `@supports (position-anchor: --anchor-name)` block. Provide a basic `position: absolute;` fallback for browsers that don't support it.\r\n5.  **Clean Up:** Remove the Popper.js or equivalent dependency from `package.json` and run `npm install` to reduce the bundle size.\r\n\r\n**Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\r\n\r\n*   **Browser Support:** The Popover API is widely supported, but CSS Anchor Positioning is very new (Chrome 125+). The fallback CSS is critical for Firefox, Safari, and older Chrome versions.\r\n*   **Complex Positioning:** For tooltips that need to flip their position based on viewport collision, the new APIs do not yet have a built-in \"auto\" placement like Popper.js. The implementation might need to handle a few common positions manually (e.g., top, bottom).\r\n*   **Styling Conflicts:** The popover element is promoted to the top layer, which can affect existing `z-index` and positioning styles. Test thoroughly to ensure it doesn't appear underneath other elements.\r\n\r\n## Iteration 1 - Tue, Apr 14, 2026  8:55:18 AM\r\nFAILED diff-guard: Add Pinterest Rich Pins metadata for room and blog pages (ID: US-159) — 14223 lines > 500 limit — attempt 1/3\r\n\r\n\r\n## Iteration US-159 - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\r\n\r\nCompleted: Add Pinterest Rich Pins metadata for room and blog pages (ID: US-159)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- `site/src/app/layout.tsx`: Added Pinterest domain verification meta tag (`p:domain_verify`) using `NEXT_PUBLIC_PINTEREST_VERIFICATION_TOKEN` env var\r\n- `site/src/app/rooms/page.tsx`: Added `other` metadata block with `og:price:amount`, `og:price:currency`, `product:price:amount`, `product:price:currency` for Pinterest Product Rich Pin\r\n- `site/src/app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx`: Fixed `publishedTime` to use `ne