{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_012QpCPPgEerWHAqiSJLmiJi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture. The key insight is:\n\nFor printing, I need to:\n1. Hide: `<header>` (navigation), `<footer>`, fixed chat widget, cookie consent, mobile booking bar, booking recovery banner, pause animations button\n\nThe cleanest approach is to add `@media print` CSS rules to globals.css. I can target:\n- `header` - semantic HTML element (Header component renders this)\n- `footer` - semantic HTML element (Footer renders this)  \n- `[role=\"dialog\"]` - ChatWidget dialog panel\n\n\n- `[aria-label=\"Chat with Pelangi Capsule Hostel FAQ assistant\"]` - ChatWidget root\n\nThe safest approach is wrapping layout components in layout.tsx with a print-hidden class rather than using fixed positioning selectors, which could break other elements. The simplest solution with minimal changes is adding a `<div className=\"print:hidden\">` wrapper around each layout component in layout.tsx, though I need to verify that Tailwind v3 supports the print variant.\n\nActually, using @media print rules directly in globals.css is cleaner—I can append about 30 lines targeting semantic selectors like `header`, `footer`, and `[role=\"dialog\"]` for the ChatWidget. The tricky parts are MobileBookingBar and BookingRecoveryBanner since they lack unique identifiers beyond Tailwind classes, so I'll need to add print:hidden wrappers to those specific components in layout.tsx instead.\n\nLooking at the components I need to hide—MobileBookingBar, BookingRecoveryBanner, ChatWidget, PauseAnimationsButton, CookieConsent, Header, and Footer—I realize the analytics providers don't render visible content so I can skip those. But Header and Footer aren't actually in layout.tsx; they're used in individual pages, so I need to check how they're structured before deciding whether to hide them via CSS or component wrappers.\n\nSince the task specifically asks for a print stylesheet for the `/book` page and booking confirmation pages, I should focus on what's actually rendered there rather than trying to hide everything globally.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":281,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1074,"cache_read_input_tokens":39612,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1074},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ebb097a-576d-4b77-a7a3-7eb4b36c845f","uuid":"c755e1cf-c7b0-443e-aab4-fa43a8f6a599"}
