{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01BqZsJQPSNqswymrVUydp1g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture. Let me plan the implementation:\n\n**Approach: Append @media print CSS to globals.css**\n\nThe plan is:\n1. Append a `@media print` block (~30 lines) to the END of globals.css\n2. No other files need to be changed\n\nThe print CSS will:\n- Hide: `header`, `footer`, `[role=\"dialog\"]` (ChatWidget), fixed elements (MobileBookingBar, CookieConsent, BookingRecoveryBanner)\n- Force: black text on white background\n- Font size: at least 12pt\n\n\n- Prevent page breaks inside booking summary blocks\n\nFor the fixed elements, I could target them with CSS selectors, but a cleaner approach would be wrapping the non-essential components in layout.tsx with a `print:hidden` class to keep the print styles contained.\n\nWrapping the components... I see the issue now—the previous attempt created a massive diff by likely duplicating entire CSS files instead of just appending the print styles. I'll stick to a minimal strategy: append only the necessary print CSS rules to globals.css and make a small wrapper change in layout.tsx to keep the diff well under 500 lines.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":852,"cache_read_input_tokens":42185,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":852},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ebb097a-576d-4b77-a7a3-7eb4b36c845f","uuid":"1253d8d5-0dd8-4794-83d8-d4d6b5055941"}
